<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sitric Silkbeard</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 970–<a href="/years/1042">1042</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Sihtric Silkbeard, Sigtrygg Silkbeard</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sitric Silkbeard was a Norse-Gaelic king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dublin">Dublin</a> from about 989 to 1036. He allied with Leinster against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brian-boru">Brian Boru</a>, and his side was defeated at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-clontarf">Battle of Clontarf</a> in 1014, although Dublin itself was not taken. He minted Dublin's first coins and founded Christ Church Cathedral around 1030.</p></div>
